{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/585079-vorpal-blade-devotion-feedback-wanted","id":585079,"title":"Vorpal Blade Devotion. Feedback Wanted","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-09T13:36:37-07:00","id":585079,"title":"Vorpal Blade Devotion. Feedback Wanted","content":"<b>Vorpal Blade (Vigor </b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, <b>Celerity </b>\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Whether for assassination, dueling, or war, blades have been used for thousands of years, in the hands of mortals and kindred alike. The best means of ending a fight is to kill in one strike, and this devotion was created to cut through armor or kindred alike. In order to use this devotion, you must have an edge weapon prepared.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> Five + Damage Rating of the Weapon<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> None<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant, or reflexive if you have the relevant Quick Draw Merit.<br /> <br /> By spending five Vitae to coat the weapon, it's blade becomes sharper that one could imagine. The first successful attack done with the blade ignores armor not generated through supernatural means, and deals aggravated damage rather than lethal due to how easily it cuts through matter. If a vampire knows this devotion but cannot spend all the required vitae at once, they may spend the required amount minus one on preceding turns, and then fully invoke it by spending the last vitae<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Alright, this is the first Devotion I've ever made. Hopefully it isn't underpowered or overpowered, but I wanted to get some criticism before I presented it to my ST. Thanks in advance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3183-shomaxt","name":"Shomaxt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T13:47:11-07:00","id":585124,"title":"","content":"You're off to a good start, but I think you might be designing a bit overcautiously. Five + [damage rating] in Vitae seems like a pretty hefty cost for a one-hit buff to me, even for dealing agg. While agg is meant to be pretty rare in 2e, it doesn't really help you end a fight any faster than lethal does, it just makes it take longer to heal. What are your design goals for this Devotion? Are you looking to create a balanced way to deal aggravated damage, or are you more interested in the thematics of the vorpal blade than the specific mechanics? Because I think there are a few ways you could improve on this idea, depending on what you want the Devotion to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T13:54:27-07:00","id":585135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/585079-vorpal-blade-devotion-feedback-wanted?p=585124#post585124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're off to a good start, but I think you might be designing a bit overcautiously. Five + [damage rating] in Vitae seems like a pretty hefty cost for a one-hit buff to me, even for dealing agg. While agg is meant to be pretty rare in 2e, it doesn't really help you end a fight any faster than lethal does, it just makes it take longer to heal. What are your design goals for this Devotion? Are you looking to create a balanced way to deal aggravated damage, or are you more interested in the thematics of the vorpal blade than the specific mechanics? Because I think there are a few ways you could improve on this idea, depending on what you want the Devotion to do.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly, if possible I'd like to go for both thematics and balanced aggravated. I like the idea of an assassination tool used to get rid of big power players, whether they be vampires or some other threat. Aggravated is the best tool for &quot;Kill it dead&quot; since there are so few ways to recover from it, that I thought it would be appropriate. What would you say is a better vitae cost for something like this? Just 5 vitae, or perhaps lower? Maybe 3?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3183-shomaxt","name":"Shomaxt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T16:26:24-07:00","id":585331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shomaxt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/585079-vorpal-blade-devotion-feedback-wanted?p=585135#post585135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, if possible I'd like to go for both thematics and balanced aggravated. I like the idea of an assassination tool used to get rid of big power players, whether they be vampires or some other threat. Aggravated is the best tool for &amp;quot;Kill it dead&amp;quot; since there are so few ways to recover from it, that I thought it would be appropriate. What would you say is a better vitae cost for something like this? Just 5 vitae, or perhaps lower? Maybe 3?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, cool, I think I see what you're going for. Its less of a buff to help take your opponent down faster and more of an insurance policy to make sure that they <i>stay</i> down. I'd agree that aggravated damage is a good way to accomplish that goal. I thought with the vorpal blade name that you might more be going for a power to remove limbs and/or heads, in which case I would have recommended using Tilts.<br /> <br /> This Devotion actually looks very similar to a power from Masquerade, one of the uses of Quietus. Maybe what you could do is have it cost the weapon's Size in Vitae to coat it, and then the next hit with it deals aggravated damage (in that case I probably wouldn't have it bypass armor). Alternatively, you could make the requirements a bit more narrow, in which case you could get away with an even lower cost. For example, maybe it only costs 1 Vitae, but can only be activated on a Killing Blow, or in a turn when you've used an active effect of both Celerity and Vigor (effectively making it require Blood Potency 3).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T00:50:56-07:00","id":587915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/585079-vorpal-blade-devotion-feedback-wanted?p=585331#post585331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, cool, I think I see what you're going for. Its less of a buff to help take your opponent down faster and more of an insurance policy to make sure that they <i>stay</i> down. I'd agree that aggravated damage is a good way to accomplish that goal. I thought with the vorpal blade name that you might more be going for a power to remove limbs and/or heads, in which case I would have recommended using Tilts.<br /> <br /> This Devotion actually looks very similar to a power from Masquerade, one of the uses of Quietus. Maybe what you could do is have it cost the weapon's Size in Vitae to coat it, and then the next hit with it deals aggravated damage (in that case I probably wouldn't have it bypass armor). Alternatively, you could make the requirements a bit more narrow, in which case you could get away with an even lower cost. For example, maybe it only costs 1 Vitae, but can only be activated on a Killing Blow, or in a turn when you've used an active effect of both Celerity and Vigor (effectively making it require Blood Potency 3).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks, I'm probably going to go with the first option. Make the cost Weapons Size + 1 or 2, just to be safe. The second option makes it a bit too narrow for my tastes. Since it doesn't cut through armor, I'll rename it from Vorpal Blade to something like &quot;Killing Edge&quot;. Seems appropriate, and my group will appreciate the Fire Emblem reference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3183-shomaxt","name":"Shomaxt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T08:00:33-07:00","id":588144,"title":"","content":"Maybe thematically have the celerity rating be higher but have it add to the damage? The thought being that the vampire is moving by at super-speed with an enhanced weapon. Seems like that should be pretty damn good at removing troublesome limbs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2060-cthulusbuttcheeks","name":"CthulusButtCheeks","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T01:01:05-07:00","id":588950,"title":"","content":"Could just add a 1-5 extra cost to add equal bonus to attack.<br /> <br /> But an Assassin can do a lot with other avenues. Look at the Fighting Styles of GMC and think about the Killing Blow rule. There are already a lot of things to help, ad them you have to think about two things:<br /> <br /> First, to not make a Devotion that ends up being less of a benefit than a damn merit.<br /> <br /> Second, that it can already benefit from similar situations.<br /> <br /> A Devotion for such purpose, I would make it to work out of normal combat, in situations similar to the ones you can create or use with stealth and Aiming.<br /> <br /> The first rule for assassination: if you're fighting, you already failed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}